                        ]
                    ]
                ],
                [
                    "description",
                    "Lazarus Group leverages targeted spearphishing emails containing malicious attachments to gain initial access to victim environments. These emails are often tailored to the target and may masquerade as job offers, business documents, financial records, security advisories, or other legitimate communications. When opened, the attachments may execute malicious code, exploit vulnerabilities, or deploy malware that enables Lazarus to establish a foothold, harvest credentials, maintain persistence, and conduct follow-on espionage or financially motivated operations within the compromised network."
