                        ],
                        [
                            "technique",
                            "T1078.004"
                        ]
                    ]
                ],
                [
                    "description",
                    "Lazarus Group leverages compromised cloud accounts to gain and maintain access to victim environments. The group targets accounts associated with cloud-based email, collaboration, storage, and productivity services, often obtaining credentials through phishing, social engineering, or other credential theft techniques. By abusing legitimate cloud accounts, Lazarus can access sensitive data, conduct reconnaissance, establish persistence, and operate within cloud environments while blending in with normal user activity, supporting its espionage, financial theft, and other cyber operations."
                ],
